    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nSame fix as #59848, for DSv4.1. Default `cpu_offload` Engram tables use `pin_memory=True`, which rounds each table up to a power of two. Register them at exact size through the existing THP helper, without huge pages. Draft: GB10 only. cc @Juntian777: could you run your #59327 lookup bench on GB200?\n\n## Claims\n\n- TP2 per-rank table: 66 \u2192 47.2 GiB host memory.\n- GB10 lookup kernel: ~1.8\u00d7 faster unsorted, 7\u201321% faster with #59327's sort.\n\n## Validation\n\nGB10, Engram lookup kernel, TP4 per-rank table, 32K tokens:\n\n| memory | host | unsorted | sorted |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `pin_memory` (before) | 33.1 GiB | 41.4 ms | 10.9 ms |\n| exact `cudaHostAlloc` | 24.9 GiB | 41.4 ms | 10.9 ms |\n| registered (this PR) | 24.3 GiB | 22.7 ms | 10.2 ms |\n\nExact size gives the memory saving; the registered memory type gives the speed. These are 4 KiB pages, not THP.\n\n`pytest tests/kernels/test_engram.py tests/distributed/test_engram_dp_shard.py`: 116 passed. The new small-page case fails on main.\n\nStill needed before un-drafting: GB200 and an E2E `cpu_offload` run.\n\n## Details\n\n- `_allocate_huge_page_storage(n)` \u2192 `_allocate_registered_storage(n, huge_pages)`, called once. The THP path and the sort are unchanged. A failed registration falls back to `pin_memory=True`.\n- CUDA only; ROCm is unchanged.\n- `use_thp` is opt-in and skips the sort, so default users still pay the rounding.\n\n<details><summary>All runs</summary>\n\n```\nTP4 (6 heads x 16Mi rows):\npinned     unsorted: 4096:5193us 8192:10355us 16384:20704us 32768:41424us\npinned     sorted:   4096:5190us 8192:4198us 16384:6680us 32768:10892us\nexact-cudaHostAlloc unsorted: 4096:5196us 8192:10367us 16384:20732us 32768:41443us\nexact-cudaHostAlloc sorted:   4096:5191us 8192:4220us 16384:6707us 32768:10919us\nregistered unsorted: 4096:2855us 8192:5695us 16384:11371us 32768:22715us\nregistered sorted:   4096:2850us 8192:3729us 16384:6173us 32768:10234us\nTP2 (12 heads x 16Mi rows):\npinned     unsorted: 4096:11851us 8192:23681us 16384:47352us 32768:94698us\nregistered unsorted: 4096:6294us 8192:12568us 16384:25120us 32768:50220us\npinned     sorted:   4096:5436us 8192:8394us 16384:13443us 32768:21951us\nregistered sorted:   4096:4492us 8192:7376us 16384:12273us 32768:20410us\n```\nMedian of 48 runs. TP4 4096 is below the sort threshold.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nDrafted with Claude; reviewed and tested by me.\n",
